# Data conversion between kibibyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kibibyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KiB to 0.0000TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0000TB; backward, converting 1TB to 976562500KiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TB yields 1464843750.0KiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(KiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(KiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TB
0.0000TB
976562500KiB
1464843750.0KiB

<<< stderr
